PS5: scan a frame out of system memory when VRAM has no room for it

amdgpu pins every frame it shows as one contiguous block of VRAM, unless the buffer was created write-combined, which a
game's swapchain is not. On a PS5 the VRAM is a fixed carve-out (vram.txt): a game that fills it leaves no room for the
next frame, the pin fails ("Failed to pin framebuffer: -ENOMEM"), gamescope aborts and the session falls back to the
desktop. Seen with Predecessor and Expedition 33, most often with 4 GB of VRAM (issues #63 and #64).

The PS5's GPU is an APU with S/G display on, so the display can read a frame from system memory. When the VRAM pin
fails with -ENOMEM, pin the frame in GTT instead. amdgpu_bo_pin() narrows a VRAM|GTT request to the buffer's preferred
VRAM, so the retry asks for GTT alone. Only for CHIP_CYAN_SKILLFISH, never for the cursor, and only with S/G display
on: amdgpu.sg_display=0 turns it off. Logged once.

Compiled; not run on a PS5. It needs system memory to be available: when RAM and swap are exhausted as well, the pin
still fails.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
index a2b8f7033..7062a5127 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
@@ -1243,6 +1243,22 @@ static int amdgpu_dm_plane_helper_prepare_fb(struct drm_plane *plane,
 
 	rbo->flags |= AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_VRAM_CONTIGUOUS;
 	r = amdgpu_bo_pin(rbo, domain);
+	/*
+	 * PS5: a frame has to be one contiguous block of VRAM, and a game that
+	 * fills the VRAM carve-out leaves none, which ends the compositor. The
+	 * display can scan out of system memory here (S/G display), so pin the
+	 * frame there instead. amdgpu_bo_pin() narrows a VRAM|GTT request to
+	 * the buffer's preferred VRAM, so ask for GTT alone. amdgpu.sg_display=0
+	 * turns this off with S/G display.
+	 */
+	if (r == -ENOMEM && plane->type != DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR &&
+	    adev->asic_type == CHIP_CYAN_SKILLFISH &&
+	    adev->mode_info.gpu_vm_support) {
+		r = amdgpu_bo_pin(rbo, AMDGPU_GEM_DOMAIN_GTT);
+		if (!r)
+			drm_info_once(adev_to_drm(adev),
+				      "no room in VRAM for a frame, scanning out of system memory\n");
+	}
 	if (unlikely(r != 0)) {
 		if (r != -ERESTARTSYS)
 			DRM_ERROR("Failed to pin framebuffer: %pe\n", ERR_PTR(r));
